		(at 36.5 60 180)
		(descr "Wurth WE-SECF 331246501860 SMT EMI contact finger, 5.0 x 2.6 x 6.0 mm, working height 3.7 to 5.8 mm (size 2460), phosphor bronze, nickel plated, tin on the soldering area. Land pattern from the Wurth data sheet 331246501860 page 1: one pad, 2.0 x 2.2 mm. Origin at the pad centre, the loop of the spring arm towards -X. The pad starts 0.65 mm from the foot end (the data sheet's figure; Wurth's STEP has 0.66), so the part spans X -3.35 to 1.65. The arm turns at the -X end and rises as a ramp back over the cage: it touches with its flat top, above the pad, X -0.4 to 1.65 (marked on F.Fab at 0.6). Let a surface slide along it towards +X. Unloaded height 6.0 mm; do not compress below 3.7 mm. Keep solder out of the spring's first bend. Generated by scripting/gen_wurth_secf_331246501860.py. 3D model: Wurth's own STEP.")
