	(footprint "Jonas:Samtec_HTSW-104-08-L-S_EdgeMount"
		(locked yes)
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "d3aa2d09-ce36-4b18-8801-b6c6347fc29f")
		(at 109.5 75 90)
		(descr "Samtec HTSW-104-08-L-S, 1x04 2.54 mm straight .025 in square post header, laid flat in a notch in the PCB edge: tails on SMT pads on the top side, insulator in the notch, posts out of the board with their tips 2.51 mm beyond the edge (flush with a Wurth 632723130112 USB-C mating face). Not a Samtec mounting style; generated by scripting/gen_samtec_htsw_edgemount.py, whose header has the reasoning. Dimensions from the Samtec print HTSW-XXX-XX-XXX-X-XX-XX-XX rev BQ: insulator 2.54 x 2.489 x 10.16 (+0.127/-0.381), pins 0.64 square, lead style -08 tail 5.08 and post 5.84. HTSW (LCP) rather than TSW: Samtec rates TSW for leaded wave soldering only. Origin on the PCB edge, +Y out of the board, pin 1 at -X. Insulator Y -5.87 to -3.33. The notch is NOT part of the footprint; it is drawn on Dwgs.User: 11.2 wide, 5.87 deep (to the insulator's rear face), relieved with R 0.5 half circles at the inner corners. Pads 1 x 5.1, 0.25 mm behind the notch wall (needs an edge clearance rule of 0.25 mm or less). Pin centre line about 0.35 mm above the board's top face; the insulator spans about -0.9 to +1.6 mm about it. 3D model: Samtec's STEP (TraceParts, HTSW-104-08-S-S, same geometry), turned 180 deg about X and offset so pin 1 is over pad 1.")
		(tags "pin header 2.54 1x04 edge mount notch horizontal SMT Samtec HTSW")
